1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,457
Krampus, the Horned Devil: he leaves presents wherever he goes, and not all of them

2
00:00:04,457 --> 00:00:04,908
are nice.

3
00:00:05,128 --> 00:00:06,408
Here's how he plays.

4
00:00:07,233 --> 00:00:11,493
Shuffle the four Krampus Presents cards into one deck and the four Santa Presents

5
00:00:11,493 --> 00:00:14,017
cards into another, and put both near the board.

6
00:00:14,237 --> 00:00:16,819
Shuffle all the Present tokens face down beside them.

7
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:22,060
Before the Finale, his usual Killer action attacks his own space, moves him towards

8
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:23,713
Victims, then throws a present.

9
00:00:24,533 --> 00:00:28,989
When you see the gift icon, roll a die and place a random face-down Present token in

10
00:00:28,989 --> 00:00:33,126
Krampus's space or next to it, using the Panic numbers on his space, just like

11
00:00:33,126 --> 00:00:34,133
panicking a Victim.

12
00:00:34,353 --> 00:00:37,276
If that space already has a Present, no new one is placed.

13
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,251
Some presents were stolen from Santa, so they're not all evil.

14
00:00:41,251 --> 00:00:45,468
During your Action phase you can open a present in your space, even partway through

15
00:00:45,468 --> 00:00:47,145
a move, resolve it, and carry on.

16
00:00:47,365 --> 00:00:51,525
Victims are less careful: any Victim in a space with a present opens it immediately,

17
00:00:51,525 --> 00:00:55,438
however they got there. And its effect applies to you, even if you're somewhere

18
00:00:55,438 --> 00:00:55,685
else.

19
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,575
Small rewards and tricks on a token apply straight away.

20
00:00:59,575 --> 00:01:04,078
A token with the Krampus icon makes you draw a Krampus Presents card, which is bad

21
00:01:04,078 --> 00:01:08,635
news. A token with Santa's icon draws a Santa Presents card, which is more powerful

22
00:01:08,635 --> 00:01:09,129
and good.

23
00:01:09,349 --> 00:01:13,799
But if a Victim opens a Santa present, discard the top Santa card with no effect:

24
00:01:13,799 --> 00:01:18,249
the Victim keeps the gift. And a Victim opening a Krampus present still draws and

25
00:01:18,249 --> 00:01:19,568
resolves a Krampus card.

26
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:23,013
Explosive Gifts makes opening presents dangerous.

27
00:01:23,013 --> 00:01:27,333
It's his most punishing power. Blood and Cookies adds more presents to the board.

28
00:01:27,553 --> 00:01:31,701
Watch for North Pole Magic, which places him straight in his target's space, Demonic

29
00:01:31,701 --> 00:01:35,848
Will, which can make his hit kill you outright, and Coal Balls, which can kill up to

30
00:01:35,848 --> 00:01:37,921
three Victims or deal three damage to you.

31
00:01:38,141 --> 00:01:41,965
The tracker doesn't have the exact wording of these cards yet, so check the card

32
00:01:41,965 --> 00:01:43,112
text when they come out.

33
00:01:43,933 --> 00:01:48,005
Bamf!: each Killer phase he's placed in the farthest target's space, then targets

34
00:01:48,005 --> 00:01:49,715
you or a Victim and attacks twice.

35
00:01:49,935 --> 00:01:54,357
Unholy Gifts sends him to the nearest present, which he eats to recover two health,

36
00:01:54,357 --> 00:01:57,874
then moves and attacks twice. Past Midnight is the hardest Finale:

37
00:01:57,874 --> 00:02:01,071
players win under forty per cent of games when it comes out.

38
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:06,006
A few tips. Open presents yourself before Victims reach them, so the good ones

39
00:02:06,006 --> 00:02:06,743
aren't wasted.

40
00:02:06,963 --> 00:02:09,437
Steer Victims away from presents near Krampus.

41
00:02:09,657 --> 00:02:13,384
He's tougher than average: players win about fifty-eight per cent of games.

42
00:02:13,384 --> 00:02:13,881
Good luck.

